Task 8.4 Implementation Summary\
I implemented Property 16: Partial data reporting accuracy which validates Requirements 6.2 - ensuring that when partial data is collected, the report correctly indicates which days have complete data and which have failures.\
\
Key Features of the Property Test:\
Comprehensive Status Validation: The test generates various data completeness scenarios (complete, partial, no data) and verifies that the ReportGenerator correctly assigns status based on:\
\
Presence of errors\
Completeness of daily breakdown (7 days expected)\
Total mention counts\
Status Logic Verification:\
\
complete: No errors AND full 7 days of data\
partial: Has errors OR incomplete data (but not zero mentions with errors)\
no data available: Zero mentions AND has errors\
Data Integrity Checks: Ensures that:\
\
All companies are included in reports regardless of data completeness\
Original data structure is preserved\
Report structure remains consistent even with partial data\
Property-Based Testing: Uses fast-check to generate 100 random test scenarios with various combinations of:\
\
Different numbers of companies (1-5)\
Various daily breakdown lengths (0-7 days)\
Random error conditions\
Different mention counts\
The test passed successfully, confirming that the ReportGenerator correctly handles partial data scenarios and accurately reports the status of each company's data completeness, fulfilling the requirements for graceful degradation and transparent error reporting.\
